1663..1736 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1737..1794 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1795..1866 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1867..1943 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1944..2020 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
2021..2095 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
2096..2174 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
2175..2217 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
